HST Office: the ribbon tooltips of the reference design (1.0.2) and the toolbar strings.

- Place: a ribbon tip (QuickHelpFlags::RichTitle) hangs 2 px under the ribbon's bottom edge (the notebookbar, or
  the popup that shows part of it: the compact ribbon's dropped page, an unfolded group), its left edge at the
  button's and at least 4 px inside the document window, instead of next to the pointer over the group captions;
  a tip of the tab row hangs under the tab row. With no room under it, it goes above the button. Lengths follow
  the display scale. Such a tip is always VCL's HelpTextWindow, also on gtk3, whose native tooltips follow the
  pointer; on a toolkit that places popups itself (Wayland) its frame is positioned by the toolkit at that point
  (SalFrame::PositionByToolkit, as menus are), and it is made anew for another button rather than moved.
- Look: a light card with the theme's menu colours and a grey border (dark in a dark theme), not the system
  tooltip look.
- Width: at most 300 px with its margins; the description wraps, a wider title keeps its width.
- Menu buttons ("Wrap Text ▾", tip "label\ndescription") and folded groups' buttons of the ribbon get the same tip,
  first line in bold (Help::ShowQuickHelp upgrades their plain tip).
- Title: where an app's design names a command differently from its label ("app_titles" of
  data/ribbon/tooltip-descriptions.json, table aHstRibbonTitles of hst-ribbon-tooltip-descriptions.patch), the bold
  line is that name and the command's shortcut in brackets; the .ui's or the table's sentence stays under it.
- The delay stays HelpSettings::GetTipDelay() (500 ms; the design's 450 ms is within its ±100 ms tolerance).
- STR_HST_RIBBON_PIN: "Pin the Toolbar (Ctrl+F1)", the pin button of the compact ribbon's dropped page
  (hst-ribbon-mockup-compact.patch), with its Vietnamese translation. User-facing Vietnamese text says
  "thanh công cụ", never "ribbon"; the vi text of the other ribbon strings is set in l10n/vi-overrides.jsonl.

